---
/**
 * Homepage. Styles here are scoped by Astro, so this redesign touches this page
 * and nothing else on the site.
 */
import Page from "@/layouts/Page.astro";
import ShieldMark from "@/components/ShieldMark.astro";
import { entity, mailHref, phoneHref } from "@/lib/entity";

const criteria = [
  ["Where", "Boise first, then the rest of the Treasure Valley: Meridian, Nampa, Eagle, Caldwell, Kuna, Star and Garden City. Also the wider southwest of Idaho."],
  ["Size", "$1 million or more in annual revenue. No upper limit."],
  ["Type", "B2B and commercial services preferred."],
  ["Age", "Five or more years in business."],
  ["Not buying", "Restaurants, retail, franchises, startups, turnarounds, businesses whose value is mostly real estate."],
];

const contrasts = [
  ["You know who is buying", "My name is on the letter and I live in Boise. You deal with me from the first call to the closing table, not an associate, and not a group that changes every quarter."],
  ["A fund has a model", "Your company has to fit it. I am not fitting your company into a model, so I can fit the purchase to your company."],
  ["A competitor wants the parts", "Usually your customer list and your best technicians, and not much else. I want the whole business, name included, running the way it runs."],
  ["Big buyers set the terms", "Who runs it, how fast you leave, when you get paid. I treat those as decisions we make together."],
];

const decisions = [
  "Who runs the company day to day",
  "Your timeline for stepping back, whether that is months or years",
  "Which employees and key people are staying, and on what terms",
  "Whether the company keeps its name, and my default is yes",
  "Your own role after close, from a clean exit to a long advisory seat",
  "How and when you get paid",
];
---
<Page pageKey="home">
  <p class="answer" slot="answer">I am Jeff Richardson, Owner of {entity.name} in Boise, Idaho. I want to buy an established business in Boise or the Treasure Valley with $1 million or more in annual revenue, preferably a B2B or commercial services company operating five or more years. If you own one and are thinking about selling, call me at {entity.contact.telephone_display}.</p>

  <section class="band">
    <h2>What I am looking for</h2>
    <dl class="criteria-list">
      {criteria.map(([term, detail]) => (
        <div class="criterion">
          <dt>{term}</dt>
          <dd>{detail}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>
    <p class="aside">
      If that describes your company, the rest of this page is for you. If you are close
      but not sure, <a href="/what-we-buy/">what we buy</a> covers the edges.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Who is buying?</h2>
    <p class="lede">Me. My name is Jeff Richardson, I live in Boise, and {entity.name} is my company.</p>
    <p>
      It exists to buy a good business in Boise and own it for a long time. Not a fund,
      not a broker, not a firm that buys to consolidate. Whatever I buy, I keep. I have
      spent several years studying Boise and Treasure Valley businesses.
    </p>
    <p>
      I have an MBA from Kellogg, worked in financial analytics at ServiceLink, part of
      Fidelity National Financial, and did strategy consulting at EY. That background
      means I can read your books and get to a fair number without wasting your time.
    </p>
    <blockquote>
      It does not mean I plan to sit in your chair on Monday morning. I am the owner, not
      the operator. Who runs the company day to day is one of the first things you and I
      work out, and it is your business that decides it, not a rule of mine.
    </blockquote>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Why sell to a named local buyer instead of a fund or a competitor?</h2>
    <p>
      Between 2021 and 2026, at least eight long-time Boise area heating and plumbing
      firms were sold to out-of-state private equity buyers. For some owners that was the
      right call. It is not the only option, and it is not the one I am offering.
    </p>
    <div class="cards">
      {contrasts.map(([head, body]) => (
        <div class="card">
          <h3>{head}</h3>
          <p>{body}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What happens to your company after you sell?</h2>
    <p>
      Before we sign anything, we agree on the things owners usually care most about:
    </p>
    <ul class="decisions">
      {decisions.map((d) => <li>{d}</li>)}
    </ul>
    <p class="aside">
      None of these are promises I can make on a website. They are options. We decide
      them together and put them in writing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="closing">
    <ShieldMark width={30} />
    <h2>How do you start?</h2>
    <p>
      One conversation. Thirty minutes, confidential, no documents. If your business is
      not a fit I will say so on that call and try to point you somewhere better suited.
    </p>
    <p class="actions">
      <a class="call" href={phoneHref}>{entity.contact.telephone_display}</a>
      <a class="mail" href={mailHref}>{entity.contact.email}</a>
    </p>
    <p class="fine">
      This offer does not expire. Thinking about selling this year, next year, or in five
      years, I would like to know you. When both sides are ready, I aim for a quick,
      professional closing within 90 days. If you are a CPA, attorney, banker or wealth
      advisor with a client who might fit, <a href="/for-advisors/">start here</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Page>

<style>
  section { margin-top: 3.5rem; }
  section > h2 { margin-top: 0; }

  .lede { font-size: 1.15em; }

  /* The buy box is the first thing a qualifying owner looks for, so it gets a
     panel of its own rather than sitting in the flow as another table. */
  .band {
    max-width: 46rem;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--rust-light);
    padding: 1.6rem 1.7rem 1.8rem;
  }
  .criteria-list { margin: 1.2rem 0 0; }
  .criterion {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 7.5rem 1fr;
    gap: 0 1.4rem;
    padding: 0.75rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .criterion:first-child { border-top: 0; padding-top: 0; }
  .criterion dt {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    color: var(--rust);
  }
  .criterion dd { margin: 0; max-width: none; }

  @media (max-width: 34rem) {
    .criterion { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.15rem; }
  }

  blockquote {
    margin: 1.6rem 0 0;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.3rem;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--rust-light);
    font-size: 1.05em;
  }
  blockquote p { margin: 0; }

  /* Four contrasts read as four things, not as one long list. */
  .cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .card {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem 1.25rem;
  }
  .card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--rust);
  }
  .card p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.98em; max-width: none; }

  .decisions { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin-top: 1.2rem; }
  .decisions li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 0.55rem 0 0.55rem 1.7rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    max-width: none;
  }
  .decisions li:first-child { border-top: 0; }
  .decisions li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0.25rem;
    top: 1.15rem;
    width: 0.45rem;
    height: 0.45rem;
    border-right: 1.5px solid var(--rust-light);
    border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--rust-light);
    transform: rotate(-45deg);
  }

  .aside { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.97em; }

  /* The page needs an ending. Ink on cream inverts, which gives the eye a place
     to stop and puts the phone number where it cannot be missed. */
  .closing {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--cream);
    padding: 2.2rem 2rem 2.4rem;
    margin-top: 4rem;
  }
  .closing h2 { color: var(--cream); border-top: 0; padding-top: 0; margin-top: 0.8rem; }
  .closing p { color: rgba(237, 230, 214, 0.86); max-width: 34rem; }
  .closing :global(svg path) { stroke: var(--cream); }
  .closing :global(svg path:nth-child(2)) { stroke: var(--rust-light); }

  .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.7rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .actions a {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.35rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 1.02rem;
  }
  .actions .call { background: var(--rust-light); color: var(--cream); }
  .actions .call:hover { background: var(--cream); color: var(--ink); }
  .actions .mail { border: 1px solid rgba(237, 230, 214, 0.45); color: var(--cream); }
  .actions .mail:hover { background: rgba(237, 230, 214, 0.12); }

  .fine { font-size: 0.94em; margin-top: 1.6rem; }
  .fine a { color: var(--cream); }
</style>
